WEBVTT

00:07.670 --> 00:09.730
<i>It's already night.</i>

00:09.730 --> 00:13.030
<i>My last overnight business trip
 to Tokyo was ages ago. It was fun.</i>

00:13.030 --> 00:16.050
<i>I'd have gotten home even sooner
 if I hadn't made that silly mistake.</i>

00:17.770 --> 00:19.900
My name is Igarashi. 
I checked out this morning.

00:20.220 --> 00:23.990
I accidentally took your hotel's 
shoehorn instead of my umbrella.

00:23.990 --> 00:25.380
I've come to return it.

00:25.380 --> 00:28.120
<i>This has never happened before!</i>

00:28.120 --> 00:30.850
<i>Well, it's not often that I 
walk around with a shoehorn,</i>

00:30.850 --> 00:32.650
<i>so it was a good experience to have.</i>

00:35.130 --> 00:36.180
<i>They dropped something.</i>

00:37.230 --> 00:38.650
<i>Is that someone from overseas?</i>

00:41.120 --> 00:43.920
Excuse me, you dropped this.

00:44.940 --> 00:46.520
Thank you so much!

02:18.490 --> 02:22.620
<b>#17 
Catalyst</b>

02:20.160 --> 02:22.180
Your Japanese is very good.

02:22.180 --> 02:24.310
Well, both of my parents are Japanese.

02:24.310 --> 02:24.950
Huh?

02:26.020 --> 02:27.650
This happens a lot.

02:29.220 --> 02:30.620
<i>I see.</i>

02:30.670 --> 02:36.090
<b>Igarashi
Motoharu</b>

02:31.070 --> 02:34.960
<i>That's a quirk I'd like to put 
into a novel at some point.</i>

02:32.050 --> 02:36.090
<b>Born June 19th   27 yrs / Writer</b>

02:36.140 --> 02:40.560
Cool and Awkward Files 05

02:38.150 --> 02:40.560
The self-absorbed genius type

02:41.510 --> 02:43.000
I'm home!

02:46.120 --> 02:47.180
Urchin.

02:46.350 --> 02:47.140
Fluff

02:47.680 --> 02:48.430
<b>Roll</b>

02:47.680 --> 02:48.430
<b>Roll</b>

02:49.150 --> 02:50.790
There, there.

02:50.790 --> 02:52.350
Were you a good house sitter?

02:53.800 --> 02:55.620
<i>At some point in my past,</i>

02:55.620 --> 02:57.950
<i>I became really interested 
in other people's stories.</i>

02:58.700 --> 03:01.200
<i>Where they came from, and what 
kind of lives they were living.</i>

03:02.200 --> 03:06.000
<i>That's probably the reason why 
I like to weave my tales.</i>

03:07.820 --> 03:11.370
<i>I think this direction will work for 
the short edition for the movie website.</i>

03:11.880 --> 03:13.390
<i>This one shouldn't take long.</i>

03:13.390 --> 03:15.280
<i>I should send the plot to Shirakawa-chan.</i>

03:16.580 --> 03:20.020
My name is Mima. I will 
be handling your project.

03:21.350 --> 03:23.760
<i>Takayuki hasn't changed.</i>

03:24.290 --> 03:27.220
<i>Actually, he's even cooler now.</i>

03:30.050 --> 03:33.400
<i>I wonder where life has 
taken him since then.</i>

03:34.700 --> 03:38.150
<i>I've written so many stories in that time.</i>

03:37.590 --> 03:38.820
Hey, guys.

03:38.820 --> 03:39.510
Yeah?

03:39.510 --> 03:40.780
Wanna go to the park later?

03:40.780 --> 03:41.640
Yeah!

03:42.780 --> 03:43.740
Hey!

03:43.740 --> 03:45.730
Igarashi Motoharu, the transfer kid!

03:46.140 --> 03:47.090
Don't go yet.

03:47.090 --> 03:48.050
Let's play.

03:48.050 --> 03:49.480
I'm not going yet.

03:49.800 --> 03:51.890
Great! Then you can come to the field with...

03:51.260 --> 03:52.310
Sorry.

03:52.310 --> 03:56.180
Whenever I transfer, the first thing 
I need to check out is the library.

03:56.180 --> 03:58.320
Uh, got it.

03:58.320 --> 04:00.800
He's super used to transferring schools.

04:00.800 --> 04:01.890
Is he a pro?

04:01.890 --> 04:04.120
They said this is his third transfer.

04:04.120 --> 04:05.390
That's really impressive.

04:06.350 --> 04:08.060
<b>Library</b>

04:06.350 --> 04:08.060
New Books

04:08.320 --> 04:10.720
<i>They've got more books than the last school.</i>

04:10.720 --> 04:12.510
<i>I should come back during my lunch breaks.</i>

04:13.000 --> 04:15.220
<i>I bet I'll have to transfer soon again anyway.</i>

04:15.220 --> 04:17.230
<i>It'd be a shame not to read here while I can.</i>

04:18.280 --> 04:21.000
<i>One day, I want to release my own books.</i>

04:21.590 --> 04:25.240
<i>Instead of spending time on friendships 
that are going to end anyway,</i>

04:23.160 --> 04:24.860
Here it comes!

04:25.510 --> 04:28.510
<i>I should use this time to 
learn as much as I can ab—</i>

04:28.280 --> 04:29.450
Thud Thud Thud

04:28.750 --> 04:29.250
<b>Startle</b>

04:31.780 --> 04:32.970
I dropped them.

04:33.650 --> 04:35.080
You dropped them?

04:36.000 --> 04:37.120
Do you need help?

04:37.120 --> 04:39.410
No. I mean, it's the librarian's job.

04:43.770 --> 04:46.460
Oh, you're the transfer student.

04:46.460 --> 04:47.580
I'm Igarashi Motoharu.

04:47.580 --> 04:48.980
You can just call me Motoharu.

04:48.980 --> 04:50.620
I'm Mima Takayuki.

04:50.620 --> 04:51.810
Takayuki.

04:52.160 --> 04:53.250
It's nice to meet you.

04:53.740 --> 04:56.230
<i>I don't particularly need friends,</i>

04:56.230 --> 04:59.170
<i>but I have gotten good at 
hitting it off with people.</i>

04:59.700 --> 05:00.940
That's amazing!

05:00.940 --> 05:04.830
So you've read everything 
here that you wanted to?

05:04.830 --> 05:07.790
Yeah. So I actually don't 
have anything to read now.

05:08.170 --> 05:10.620
I want to be a writer when I grow up.

05:10.620 --> 05:14.000
If I were an adult, I could have 
just given you a book I'd written.

05:14.000 --> 05:15.190
Why not now?

05:15.190 --> 05:16.080
Huh?

05:16.700 --> 05:18.420
Why not just write something now?

05:18.730 --> 05:21.120
Why do you have to wait until you grow up?

05:24.520 --> 05:27.300
Even if I did, nobody would read it.

05:27.300 --> 05:30.590
So it never goes further than 
knocking around in my head.

05:30.920 --> 05:32.450
My parents are always really busy,

05:32.450 --> 05:35.010
and my friends keep changing 
from all the transfers.

05:35.250 --> 05:39.240
But if I grow up and release a book, 
they'll carry it in bookstores.

05:39.240 --> 05:44.530
So that's why I thought I should 
just focus on studying right now...

05:42.230 --> 05:45.190
<b>A person who has 
nothing to read
and too much time 
on their hands</b>

05:45.430 --> 05:47.900
Wait, would you actually read 
it if I wrote something?!

05:47.900 --> 05:48.930
I would.

05:48.930 --> 05:51.430
I don't have anything to read right now.

05:51.430 --> 05:53.360
So that's the reason, huh.

05:54.440 --> 05:56.080
Then I'll start writing right now.

05:56.650 --> 05:58.040
Wow.

05:59.380 --> 06:01.590
What kind of things do you think about?

06:01.590 --> 06:02.560
Novels.

06:03.690 --> 06:06.250
So the protagonist would be...

06:07.160 --> 06:08.270
...would be...

06:08.920 --> 06:12.220
<i>I always have so many ideas in my head,</i>

06:12.220 --> 06:14.420
<i>but when it's time to actually 
write, it's difficult.</i>

06:15.620 --> 06:17.270
<i>What are people like, anyway?</i>

06:18.070 --> 06:20.780
<i>I've run into so many different people,</i>

06:20.780 --> 06:22.990
<i>but all the memories I have 
of them seem identical.</i>

06:23.350 --> 06:26.630
<i>They didn't hate me, 
nor did they like me.</i>

06:28.890 --> 06:30.690
Why don't you make yourself 
the main character?

06:31.920 --> 06:33.200
I can't do that!

06:33.200 --> 06:34.210
Why not?

06:34.210 --> 06:36.610
I'm not the main-character type.

06:38.580 --> 06:41.180
I got it! I'll make you the protagonist!

06:41.180 --> 06:43.600
But I'm not that type either.

06:43.600 --> 06:46.290
You're going to be reading 
it, so you work just fine.

06:46.290 --> 06:48.130
So you have...

06:48.390 --> 06:50.340
sleepy-looking eyes,

06:50.340 --> 06:51.950
a brooding aura,

06:52.390 --> 06:54.050
and a love for books.

06:54.050 --> 06:54.890
Plus...

06:56.510 --> 06:58.020
You're cool, but awkward.

06:58.400 --> 07:01.740
Now that that's decided, I'm going to 
have to get to know you better.

07:01.740 --> 07:02.440
Time for research!

07:02.880 --> 07:04.460
So what's your favorite food?

07:04.460 --> 07:05.570
Your favorite color?

07:06.290 --> 07:08.030
Come on, this is important.

07:08.410 --> 07:10.730
I like sushi and deep blue.

07:10.730 --> 07:12.440
What makes you happy?

07:12.740 --> 07:14.650
Going to the movies makes me happy.

07:15.040 --> 07:18.490
<i>Huh? This is so fun.</i>

07:19.280 --> 07:22.340
<i>There isn't a single book 
out there about Takayuki.</i>

07:22.850 --> 07:26.300
<i>I thought you could find everything 
you could possibly learn in books.</i>

07:26.300 --> 07:27.820
<i>But if you want to learn about a person,</i>

07:27.820 --> 07:29.880
<i>there's no other way than to 
really interact with them.</i>

07:30.360 --> 07:32.950
<i>You can't write about people 
if you don't learn about them.</i>

07:33.840 --> 07:35.300
Favorite food -> Sushi



Favorite color -> Deep blue
 
What makes you happy? -> 


Going to the movies

07:33.840 --> 07:35.300
Has sleepy eyes
 
Brooding aura


Likes to read books



Cool, but awkward

07:34.370 --> 07:35.300
Yay!

07:35.850 --> 07:37.990
I've made my very first protagonist!

07:37.990 --> 07:41.140
But now you've got to 
think of a story, right?

07:41.140 --> 07:43.270
Writing a novel must be hard.

07:43.270 --> 07:45.410
But I feel like I can do it now.

07:45.410 --> 07:46.860
Thanks a lot, Takayuki.

07:46.860 --> 07:48.650
I'll go write it myself.

07:49.270 --> 07:51.160
Promise me you'll read it when I'm done!

07:51.160 --> 07:52.200
Okay.

07:52.200 --> 07:53.630
Look forward to it.

07:53.630 --> 07:54.560
Bye!

07:54.450 --> 07:55.320
<b>Slam</b>

07:54.930 --> 07:57.170
<i>He kind of resolved that all in his head...</i>

07:59.040 --> 07:59.910
<b>Big</b>

07:59.040 --> 07:59.910
<b>Big</b>

07:59.500 --> 08:01.470
<i>That's a big thing to leave behind.</i>

08:02.940 --> 08:04.610
<i>Motoharu screws up, too.</i>

08:06.670 --> 08:08.820
Hey, Igarashi Motoharu!

08:09.760 --> 08:12.100
If you're free now, come on over.

08:13.130 --> 08:16.550
We still don't know anything about you.

08:18.600 --> 08:19.530
Okay!

08:19.530 --> 08:21.670
I want to get to know all of you, too.

08:26.270 --> 08:28.690
<i>I thought he was going home, 
but he's playing ball.</i>

08:29.280 --> 08:31.040
<i>Running on his own clock, I guess.</i>

08:32.010 --> 08:34.340
Oh, Takayuki, you're still here too.

08:34.340 --> 08:35.490
Come on over!

08:35.490 --> 08:37.390
We need more players.

08:37.390 --> 08:38.640
Sure.

08:38.640 --> 08:39.990
<i>I wanted to go home.</i>

08:43.540 --> 08:46.170
<i>Talk about a trip down memory lane.</i>

08:46.480 --> 08:49.120
<i>Maybe it's because I met Takayuki again.</i>

08:49.540 --> 08:53.150
<i>Who knows if he still remembers me.</i>

08:53.960 --> 08:56.590
<i>I guess he lives in Tokyo now.</i>

08:57.370 --> 09:00.220
<i>I can do everything I need to in Kyoto,</i>

09:00.220 --> 09:02.130
<i>but thanks to a certain person,</i>

09:02.130 --> 09:04.350
<i>I'm finally starting to 
see the value of Tokyo.</i>

09:07.060 --> 09:09.010
Have you been there this whole time?

09:09.010 --> 09:10.030
You're so cute.

09:10.760 --> 09:11.680
Thanks for waiting.

09:11.680 --> 09:12.490
I'm done.

09:14.700 --> 09:16.410
<b></b>Pants he discarded on the ground

09:20.050 --> 09:21.250
I'll move to Tokyo.

09:21.950 --> 09:24.490
<i>Now that a certain man has given me a nudge,</i>

09:25.040 --> 09:27.770
<i>I wonder what kind of encounters 
await me once I get there.</i>

09:27.770 --> 09:29.550
<i>Maybe they're worth looking forward to.</i>

10:59.970 --> 11:04.970
<b>Coming up next</b>

10:59.970 --> 11:04.970
<b>Takayuki and Motoharu</b>

11:04.980 --> 11:09.970
<b>We hope you'll tune in again!</b>

11:04.980 --> 11:09.970
<b>We hope you'll tune in again!</b>
